# Test: an operator raising the eBGP distance is accepted and takes effect.
# VALIDATES: AC-2 -- a partial block keeps the other five declared values.
# VALIDATES: AC-6 -- a changed distance is what the daemon runs on.
#
# WHAT THIS PROVES AND WHAT IT DOES NOT. It drives the real binary over the real
# config path, so it proves the container parses, that a single named leaf is
# accepted beside five defaulted ones, and that the daemon starts on it. It does
# NOT prove an OSPF route beats an eBGP one at distance 250: that needs two
# protocols holding one prefix, which is a QEMU scenario rather than a config
# case. TestBgpStampsTheDeclaredDistanceNotItsOwn
# (internal/component/bgp/plugins/rib/rib_bestchange_test.go) covers the half
# this cannot reach, and was observed RED at 0x14 where 0xfa was required.

stdin=dist-override:terminator=EOF_OVERRIDE
rib {
	distance {
		ebgp 250;
	}
}
EOF_OVERRIDE

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=dist-override:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=configuration valid

# The other five keep their declared values: a partial block is not a whole one.
stdin=dist-override-full:terminator=EOF_FULL
rib {
	distance {
		ebgp 250;
		ospf 110;
	}
}
EOF_FULL

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=dist-override-full:exit=0
expect=exit:code=0
